avro-linux (1.3.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Output as ANSI (Bijoy): port of Avro Keyboard for Windows' Unicode to
    Bijoy converter (TUnicodeToBijoy2000), so conjuncts and vowel signs come
    out as on Windows (প্রোগ্রাম = †cÖvMÖvg, স্কুল = ¯‹zj, শব্দ = kã) instead
    of a visible "&". A word still being typed is shown and kept in Bijoy
    when focus moves away. য় ড় ঢ় written as letter + nukta convert too.
  * Unicode ↔ Bijoy converter: "Convert to Unicode" works (it called a
    function that does not exist) and reads Bijoy text back properly; the
    window uses the same converter as the engine.
  * Setup wizard (avro-setup): no longer crashes on start; installs only the
    avro-linux package it was given or that the user picks (it searched the
    current folder and /tmp before), with apt and without a shell; no
    automatic restart (logging out is enough); the "Start Avro TopBar" and
    "Add Avro to my keyboard list" choices work. It no longer registers
    itself as the program that opens every .deb file.
  * Installation changes no user's settings: the maintainer script no longer
    rewrites every user's input sources (with a broken value for users who
    had some) or restarts their IBus, and no schema override changes
    everyone's default keyboards. The TopBar offers once to add Avro to the
    keyboard list; Avro Doctor's Auto-Fix and avro-setup can do it.
  * TopBar: no longer puts Avro back into the keyboard list at every start or
    hides the IBus panel; starts IBus only when it is not running (without
    disabling its panel). In the "Output as ANSI" question Enter means OK.
  * "Start Avro TopBar when I log in" can be turned off: a Hidden=true entry
    in ~/.config/autostart overrides the system-wide one. Autostart entries
    have TryExec, so they are ignored once Avro is uninstalled.
  * Avro Doctor: "Copy Report" works; typing English is not reported as a
    problem; reports whether Avro is in the keyboard list; reads Bengali font
    names correctly; checks this session's IBus; Auto-Fix no longer switches
    the keyboard or the Bangla mode, or disables the IBus panel.
  * KDE Plasma (Wayland): Avro types there only when IBus Wayland is KWin's
    input method (System Settings → Keyboard → Virtual Keyboard). Avro Doctor
    reports it; when no input method is chosen, Auto-Fix, the TopBar's
    one-time question and avro-setup choose IBus Wayland. Another input
    method (fcitx, Maliit) is never replaced.
  * Avro Pad: zoom works and the editor gets its intended font (GTK 3 ignores
    a font size on the "text" node); its own composition works while the
    Avro IBus keyboard is on.
  * Avro Mouse: য় ড় ঢ় are one character each; Backspace removes a letter
    with its nukta.
  * The IBus variables in /etc/profile.d and Plasma's env are set only when
    no input method framework is chosen yet (never over fcitx), and not on
    GNOME or KDE Wayland. Files in /etc are conffiles.
  * Windows show their own title in the taskbar (Avro Pad, Avro Converter, …);
    no more "g_set_application_name() called multiple times" warnings; the
    splash screen no longer renames the TopBar.
  * Tests: the packaging test checks again that the maintainer scripts leave
    users' input settings alone (and now really fails when they do not); the
    Bengali digit check is back; the live engine test runs its IBus on a
    private D-Bus again; new Bijoy converter tests with যুক্তবর্ণ words.

 -- MD Shifat Bin Siddique Urfi and MD Mehedi Hasan <hello@msbsu.com>  Sun, 04 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0600

avro-linux (1.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Attribution updated: "Remastered by MD Shifat Bin Siddique Urfi
    (DMC, K-79) and MD Mehedi Hasan (CSE 21, BUET)" across all apps, splash,
    About dialogs, status bars, CLI output, and headers.
  * Version bumped to 1.3.0 across all packages, launchers, and documentation.
  * The fixed keyboard layouts of Avro Keyboard 5, typed by the Avro engine
    itself: Avro Easy, Bornona, Munir Optima, National (Jatiya) and Probhat,
    converted from the Windows layout files (scripts/import-avrolayout.py).
    They work wherever Avro Phonetic works, Wayland included, and F12
    switches between Bangla and English with all of them.
  * The fixed layout typing rules of Avro Keyboard: Modern Style Typing with
    "Old Style Reph", "Automatic Vowel Forming" and "Automatically fix
    Chandrabindu position", and Old Style Typing (e, i and oi kars typed
    before the consonant); Bangla digits on the number pad; Right Alt types
    the AltGr characters.
  * TopBar: Avro's layouts first in the layout menu, the system's Bangla XKB
    layouts in a submenu; Fixed Keyboard Layout Options in the Tools menu;
    the layout's credits in "About current keyboard layout"; autostart on login.
  * Layout Viewer: draws the fixed layouts with a Normal and an AltGr view,
    follows the active layout, "Show on Top", "About layout..."; takes a
    layout name (avro-layout national).
  * Preferences: a Keyboard Layouts tab with the layout and its options.
  * Fixed Bengali typing in Electron apps (VS Code): engine sends synthetic
    focus_in / register_properties sequence after engine enable(), and uses
    IBus.PreeditFocusMode.COMMIT to ensure inline preedit works reliably.
  * Fixed window maximize/minimize custom buttons across standalone suite.
  * Avro Doctor: added 8 new diagnostic checks (IBus version, ibus-avro component
    file, embed-preedit-text setting, GNOME input sources, locale, IBus version,
    env-var validation with auto-fix status).
  * Safe GSettings schema lookup in Doctor and engine (prevents crashing if missing).
  * Full clean build verified: all tests pass.

 -- MD Shifat Bin Siddique Urfi <hello@msbsu.com>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0600

avro-linux (1.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New Avro TopBar, re-created from Avro Keyboard 5 for Windows: the 285x30
    bar with the অ menu, বাংলা / English mode button and keyboard-layout strip,
    Layout Viewer, Avro Mouse, Tools, Web, Help and power button, with the
    Windows menus and tooltips. Original Cairo artwork, scaled to the DPI.
  * Real keyboard layouts in the TopBar: Avro Phonetic plus the Bangla XKB
    layouts in IBus (National (Jatiya), Probhat, Bornona first); switching
    also applies the X keyboard layout, like `ibus engine`. Replaces the old
    layout list whose entries did nothing.
  * The TopBar never takes focus, stays on top on every workspace, drags by
    the logo with a 32 px magnetic snap, remembers its X position, fades to
    a transparency level when idle, hides to the system tray (click toggles
    the mode, double-click restores), runs once per session and accepts the
    commands toggle, bn, sys, minimize and restore.
  * Four TopBar skins and the Windows TopBar options (transparency, power
    button action, start-up mode, start on login) in Preferences -> TopBar.
  * Fixed the old TopBar's emoji icons showing as boxes without an emoji font.
  * The version number now lives only in the Makefile; About boxes, the IBus
    component and the package read it from there (they showed 1.0.0).
  * Launchers no longer load modules from ./src of the current directory.
  * Recommends gkbd-capplet for the fixed-layout Layout Viewer.

