avro-linux (1.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Added the Windows-style Avro Preview Window: a floating window at the text
    cursor with the typed English text (yellow row) and the Bangla suggestions
    (selected word in blue). Drawn in-process by the engine as a focus-less
    X11 popup, so it updates on every key and never steals focus.
  * Preview Window: click a word to insert it, drag the title bar or click the
    pin to keep it in place, classic (Windows) and dark themes.
  * The preview is now on by default; the desktop IBus candidate panel is used
    on GNOME Wayland (with the typed text shown above a vertical list).
  * Fixed Bangla rendering: ship a fontconfig rule that prefers Noto Sans/Serif
    Bengali over Lohit Bengali and Mukti, whose headline (matra) breaks over
    letters such as আ and ম. Recommends fonts-noto-core.
  * Fixed Shift+Tab (ISO_Left_Tab) not cycling suggestions backwards.
  * F12, the mode switch and switching keyboards now keep the word being typed
    instead of discarding it.
  * Tab, arrows and Enter (with "Enter inserts new line") finish the word and
    then reach the application, instead of inserting literal tab/newline text.
  * Never compose in password fields, so typed text is not shown in the preview.
  * Fixed lookup-table labels repeating ("1." after "3.") as words got longer.
  * Removed the per-keystroke Unix socket IPC to the separate avro-preview
    process; avro-preview is now a helper to turn the preview on/off or show
    a demo (avro-preview --demo).

 -- MD Shifat Bin Siddique Urfi <hello@msbsu.com>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0600

avro-linux (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Remastered release of Avro Linux by MD Shifat Bin Siddique Urfi.
  * Added floating sticky always-on-top Windows-style Avro TopBar with full options.
  * Added standalone Avro Pad text editor with live inline Bengali phonetic typing.
  * Added 100% roundtrip Unicode <-> Bijoy (SutonnyMJ) Converter.
  * Added interactive visual Keyboard Layout Viewer.
  * Fixed F12 key handling to toggle between Bangla and English mode.
  * Modernized IBus engine key event processing for Wayland and modern Linux distributions (Ubuntu 24.04/26.04, Debian 12/13).
  * Automated IBus cache registration in postinst/postrm.
  * Added Avro Doctor diagnostic health check and interactive live self-test tool (avro-doctor CLI and GUI).
  * Added dedicated non-focus-stealing floating candidate & preview window (avro-preview).
  * Implemented decoupled local Unix socket IPC between engine and UI without Wayland focus theft.
  * Added Tab / Shift+Tab candidate cycling and 1-9 direct candidate numeric accelerators.
  * Enhanced Avro TopBar with Dock type hint and non-focus-stealing buttons to stay sticky and upper than all windows.
  * Comprehensive developer and architecture documentation (windows-avro-behavior.md, linux-input-architecture.md, desktop-integration.md, compatibility-matrix.md).
  * Expanded automated test suite with 11 passing suites and 0 failures.

